{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And when a woman has a discharge of blood.</b> This teaches the laws of the menstruant and the zavah, and it requires the zavah to bring a sin-offering and a burnt-offering. Thereby it testifies that this will not occur among the daughters of His people otherwise than to alert them concerning the rebellion that preceded — both in deed and in thought. For it is indeed the multiplication of the punishment with which He punished Eve for her action and her thought, which is included in His saying: הַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה עִצְּבוֹנֵךְ (Genesis 3:16). Therefore it is fitting that she count seven clean days, until a spirit of repentance and purification rests upon her, and then she immerses and attains atonement — by the sin-offering for the evil deed, and by the burnt-offering for the thought."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:22.391428018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}